{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S6: Transition replay fallback for invalid direct Jira transitions\n\n## Context / Problem\nWhen a Jira workflow forbids the DIRECT end-state transition rebar wants (e.g.\n`open -> done` where the workflow only allows `open -> in_progress -> done`), the\noutbound status sync fails and the ticket drifts. Today the status field flows\n`update_one` -> `client.update_issue(status=...)` -> `transition_issue_by_name`.\nCloud: `AcliClient.transition_issue_by_name` (`adapters/jira/acli.py:489`) GETs the\nissue's available transitions, matches the target, POSTs one hop, and raises\n`RuntimeError` when none reach the target (`acli.py:536`) or `urllib.error.HTTPError`\non a non-2xx POST. DC: `JiraDataCenterTransport.transition_issue_by_name`\n(`adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:229`) delegates to\n`transitions.transition_to_status` -> `resolve_transition`, which raises **`ValueError`**\nwhen no transition reaches the target (`transitions.py:104`) — and the illegal-from-\ncurrent-state case is `IllegalTransitionError`, a `ValueError` subclass deliberately\nNOT an `HTTPError` (`transitions.py:33-36`). The direct path executes ONE hop and\ngives up; `dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update` (`dispatch_one.py` ~L618-650)\nturns the failure into comment-fallback + drift (`result=None`).\n\nThis story replays rebar's REAL recorded status hops so the end state is reached via\nallowed intermediate hops. Self-healing (inventing hops Jira allows but rebar never\ntook) is OUT of scope — replay only mirrors hops that actually happened in rebar.\n\n## Approach\n1. **Data source — the recorded hop sequence (grounded).** rebar is event-sourced:\n   every transition appends an append-only `STATUS` event under\n   `<tracker>/<local_id>/<timestamp>-STATUS.json`, written by `rebar._commands.txn`\n   (`txn.py` ~L330) with `event_type=\"STATUS\"` and\n   `data={\"status\":<target>,\"current_status\":<from>,\"parent_status_uuid\":…}`. Event\n   files sort by filename = chronological — the same ordering `reduce_ticket` replays\n   in (`rebar/reducer/_api.py:138`) and `txn._parent_status_uuid` relies on\n   (`txn.py:105`, `f.endswith(\"-STATUS.json\")`). Reading each event's `data[\"status\"]`\n   in filename order yields rebar's real ordered hops — no invention. The mutation\n   carries the ticket id as `mutation[\"local_id\"]` (`dispatch_one.py:128`); the\n   tracker dir is `config.tracker_dir(repo_root)`.\n   NEW helper `recorded_status_hops(local_id, tracker) -> list[str]` globs\n   `*-STATUS.json`, sorts by filename, and returns the ordered targets FORWARD-mapped\n   local->Jira via `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` (`adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py:78-86`).\n   The whole sequence therefore lives in **Jira-name space**, e.g. `[\"To Do\",\n   \"In Progress\",\"Done\"]`.\n\n2. **Ambiguity-free resume point — NO inverse map.** `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` is\n   NON-INJECTIVE (`value_maps.py:78-86`: `In Progress` <- {in_progress, blocked};\n   `Done` <- {closed, cancelled, deleted}), so it has no well-defined inverse and a\n   reverse lookup could mislocate the resume index. We NEVER invert it. Instead read\n   the issue's current status with the existing required member\n   `client.get_issue(remote_id)` (`_backend.py` CRUD surface), take\n   `fields.status.name` (a Jira NAME), and match it DIRECTLY against the forward-mapped\n   Jira-name hop list from (1) — comparison stays entirely in Jira-name space.\n   Deterministic tie-break: if the current Jira name appears at multiple positions\n   (e.g. two hops both map to `In Progress`), anchor on the LAST (highest-index)\n   match — Jira is at its most-recently-synced state — and replay the hops AFTER it.\n   If the current Jira name matches NO position, abort (see 3). No local status is\n   ever reconstructed from a Jira name.\n\n3. **Replay uses ONLY the existing seam.** The transport exposes NO\n   list-available-transitions method; the required member it DOES expose is\n   `TicketTransport.transition_issue_by_name(remote_id, target_status)`\n   (`_backend.py:250`, in `_REQUIRED_TRANSPORT_MEMBERS` `_backend.py:141`). **No new\n   transport method is added.** Replay calls `transition_issue_by_name` once per\n   remaining Jira-name hop, in order; each call re-fetches the now-current per-issue\n   transitions and executes the next legal hop, reaching the end state.\n\n4. **Failure mode — grounded, covers BOTH implementors, no field metadata.** The\n   per-transition required-field abort is DROPPED (the transitions fetch requests no\n   field metadata and the transport has no method for it). Instead, replay aborts if\n   ANY hop raises — catching the UNION of what both named implementors raise:\n   `RuntimeError` (acli no-transition, `acli.py:536`), `ValueError` (DC no-transition\n   AND its `IllegalTransitionError` subclass, `transitions.py:33,104`), and\n   `urllib.error.HTTPError`/`JiraAPIError`/`BackendHTTPError` (a 400, incl. an\n   un-fillable required field surfacing on the POST). On abort it falls through to the\n   EXISTING comment-fallback + drift arm (`dispatch_one.py` ~L622, `result=None`),\n   exactly as today. No partial hop is retried.\n\n5. **Wiring.** In `_update_one_scalar_update`, widen the failure catch so the\n   illegal-direct case on EITHER backend (`JiraAPIError` 400 today, PLUS the\n   pre-execute `RuntimeError`/`ValueError`) calls the new `replay_transition(...)`\n   FIRST; only if replay returns False does the current comment-fallback run.\n\n## Scope\n- NEW `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/transition_replay.py`:\n  `recorded_status_hops()`, `replay_transition(client, remote_id, local_id, tracker,\n  target_status)`. Keeps `dispatch_one.py` (currently **678 LOC**, hard cap 800 —\n  `AGENTS.md` module-size policy) under the cap; only a small call site is added there.\n- EDIT `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py`: in\n  `_update_one_scalar_update`, invoke `replay_transition` before the existing\n  comment-fallback and widen the except to the union in (4); import the helper.\n- No transport/protocol change; no new required member.\n\n## Testing\nNEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_transition_replay.py` with fake Cloud and DC\ntransports recording `transition_issue_by_name` calls (the DC fake raising\n`ValueError`/`IllegalTransitionError`, the Cloud fake raising `RuntimeError`) and an\non-disk tracker of `*-STATUS.json` events.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_replay_walks_recorded_intermediate_hops` — recorded hops\n  open->in_progress->closed, workflow rejecting the direct end hop: the transport\n  receives `transition_issue_by_name(\"In Progress\")` then `(\"Done\")`, in order.\n- [ ] `test_replay_resume_point_matches_in_jira_name_space` — with `get_issue`\n  reporting current Jira status \"In Progress\", only the \"Done\" hop is replayed; the\n  resume index is found WITHOUT inverting `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`.\n- [ ] `test_replay_duplicate_jira_name_anchors_on_last_occurrence` — a hop list with\n  \"In Progress\" at two positions resumes after the LAST match (deterministic tie-break).\n- [ ] `test_replay_never_invents_unrecorded_hops` — a hop absent from the recorded\n  STATUS sequence is never sent, even if it would be a legal Jira transition.\n- [ ] `test_replay_aborts_and_drifts_on_illegal_hop` — PARAMETRIZED over BOTH\n  backends: a mid-chain hop raising `RuntimeError` (Cloud/acli) AND one raising\n  `IllegalTransitionError`/`ValueError` (DC) each abort replay and run the existing\n  comment-fallback (`result is None`, no further hops attempted).\n- [ ] `test_recorded_status_hops_orders_by_filename` — `recorded_status_hops` returns\n  the STATUS `data[\"status\"]` targets in filename order, forward-mapped to Jira names.\n- [ ] `test_replay_aborts_when_current_status_not_in_sequence` — an out-of-band Jira\n  status name absent from the forward-mapped hop list aborts to drift, not a guess.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787354805901836001,"uuid":"3d7931c5-dba2-4133-b728-4b62f81989b4"}